      <h2 data-i18n="aboutStoryTitle">The Story</h2>
      <p data-i18n="aboutStoryP1">I founded MotivaHub in 2025 after spending eight months writing my first book, but I failed to launch it because of self-sabotage. I had the content. I had the plan. After many attempts that did not go as I had hoped, I began to understand that failure was not the end, but part of the journey. With each attempt, I learned more about myself, about discipline, and about the need to build a system that helps me keep going.</p>

      <p data-i18n="aboutStoryP2">That failure taught me more than any success could have taught me. It taught me that discipline is not about motivation, but about designing systems, building identity, and showing up even when there is no accountability.</p>

      <p data-i18n="aboutStoryP3">That is where the idea for MotivaHub began: to build something that helps people turn these lessons into systems, habits, and practices they can continue even when motivation disappears.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="aboutWriteAboutTitle">What I Write About</h2>
      <p data-i18n="aboutWriteAboutP1">I write about the things I have tested personally: habits, discipline, productivity, mindset, and the long game. Every article on this site is based on real experiments, real failures, and real results.</p>

      <p data-i18n="aboutWriteAboutP2">I do not write theory. I write about what worked, what did not work, and what I learned from both.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="aboutMissionTitle">The Mission</h2>
      <p data-i18n="aboutMissionP1">Motiva Hub is a premium editorial sanctuary for the disciplined mind. It is not a motivation factory. It is a place for people who want to build systems that last, habits that stick, and identities that matter.</p>

      <p data-i18n="aboutMissionP2">The mission is simple: help you build the thing that builds everything else — yourself.</p>

